       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day of acetaminophen. That is in the range that can cause acute liver failure and death, even in a 70 kg adult with normal liver function. No indication I know of calls for this dose, and you haven't given a rationale.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum). Lower doses also work.\n- **Add a note to the order** if you want one, such as an indication or a PRN instruction.\n- **Suggest you talk to pharmacy** if you think this dose is intended for a special situation. If the order came from a protocol or a colleague, check it first, because it may be a transcription error such as 500 mg.\n\nIf a dose above 4 g/day is clinically justified, it should go through pharmacy and attending review, not routine order entry. Tell me which standard dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
